Z||000000||Earl||11-15-2001||04:38 AM||||   Has anyone had a problem like this. I was just driving down the road and when I went to stop and depressed the clutch It felt strange and the engine died I had to start the car in gear to get out of the intersection .Like I lost my master cyl.<BR>when I atempted to shift to 2nd I depressed the clutch it came back but the the clutch stayed disengaged and never engaged again .<BR>  I had no slipping befor and every thing was working great, even though it has 140k on it I am getting ready to tear it apart and Ill probibly rebuild the motor while I have it out .But I was wondering if anyone has had this happen or has any Idea of what would cause this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-16-2001||12:06 AM||||Is it hard to get into first when you come to a stop?  And all the other gear changes are anything but smooth?  It might be the throw-out bearing.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||11-16-2001||12:22 AM||||Is the pedal stiff/rock hard when you depress it?  It's possible that the springs on the pressure plate gave way and the T.O. bearing kept on going.  It's not uncommon, especially with a ton of miles.<P>I bought an '87 SE several years ago with a bad clutch.  As we were attempting to start it up (so I could hear it run) it went "pop" and the clutch let go (T.O. bearing went through the pressure plate).<P>It sounds like you will have a nice project!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Earl||11-16-2001||04:47 AM||||  It isn't hard to put into 1st it goes in all gears fine. It just wont go anywhere at all no noise nothing engine runs good though .its like the input shaft sheard off or some thing .<BR>  If the TOB went through the pressure plate that would explane it I will post s reply when I find out..<P>Thanks for the help and comments.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tesmith66||11-16-2001||09:09 AM||||Same thing happened to me.<P>T/O bearing went THROUGH the pressure plate.<P>Ouch.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
